 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Lines in a triangle",
   "col": "L",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "fig",
     "ref": "lines",
     "caption": "**Median**: to the middle of the opposite side. **Altitude**: at $90°$ to the opposite side (outside the triangle when the angle is obtuse). **Bisector**: splits the angle in half."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Angles",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "rules",
     "head": [
      "Rule",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "The angles add up to $180°$",
       "$50°,\\ 60° \\Rightarrow 70°$"
      ],
      [
       "At most one right or obtuse angle",
       "$100°$ and $95°$: impossible"
      ],
      [
       "Exterior angle $=$ the two far angles",
       "$47°+68°=115°$"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "fig",
     "ref": "ext",
     "caption": "The exterior angle saves a step."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Sides",
   "col": "L",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "fig",
     "ref": "side",
     "caption": "The longest side faces the largest angle; the shortest side faces the smallest."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "**Two sides together are longer than the third.** So a third side is **between the difference and the sum**: sides $4$ and $9$ give $5<c<13$."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Special triangles",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "rules",
     "head": [
      "Triangle",
      "What you know"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Isosceles",
       "Equal base angles; the line from the top is a median, altitude and bisector at once"
      ],
      [
       "Equilateral",
       "All angles $60°$; area $\\frac{a^2\\sqrt3}{4}$"
      ],
      [
       "Right",
       "The hypotenuse is the longest side; the median to it is half of it"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Pythagoras",
   "col": "L",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "Only in a **right** triangle: $a^2+b^2=c^2$, $c$ = the hypotenuse. Add to find $c$, subtract to find a leg: $6,8\\Rightarrow10$; $\\ 13,5\\Rightarrow12$."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "**Triples**: $3,4,5$ and $5,12,13$ and their multiples ($9,12,15$; $\\ 15,36,39$). Check which side is the hypotenuse."
    },
    {
     "type": "fig",
     "ref": "g025",
     "caption": "Triangle by triangle: each triple gives the next side."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Gold and silver",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "cols",
     "cols": [
      [
       {
        "type": "fig",
        "ref": "gold",
        "caption": "**Gold** $30°$-$60°$-$90°$: $a,\\ a\\sqrt3,\\ 2a$"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "type": "fig",
        "ref": "silver",
        "caption": "**Silver** $45°$-$45°$-$90°$: $a,\\ a,\\ a\\sqrt2$"
       }
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "Divide by a root: $\\frac{9}{\\sqrt3}=3\\sqrt3$; $\\ \\frac{18}{\\sqrt2}=9\\sqrt2$."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Area",
   "span": "full",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "cols",
     "cols": [
      [
       {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "$S=\\frac{\\text{side}\\times\\text{its altitude}}{2}$. Any side works, with **its own** altitude: $\\frac{12\\cdot6}{2}=\\frac{9\\cdot8}{2}=36$."
       },
       {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Right triangle: $\\text{leg}\\times\\text{leg}=\\text{hypotenuse}\\times\\text{altitude}$."
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "**A median halves the area.** Same base and same height mean the same area. Triangles between parallel lines share their height."
       },
       {
        "type": "fig",
        "ref": "g017",
        "caption": "Same height $\\Rightarrow$ the areas are in the ratio of the bases."
       }
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Before each question, ask",
   "class": "check",
   "col": "L",
   "blocks": [
